The entry sequence is explicit: identify registration; authenticate/admit generated event; validate
the exact payload/schema; traverse the compiled source path; validate terminal ObserverId role;
construct the exact IDN roster path; perform its required read; expose only ResolvedCharacterSubject;
then run formation. Forged M1 fails before any roster read. Nested canonical extraction produces no
ActualReadRecord or transition-visible source accessor; only the roster read is an authoritative
state read. M4b's future composite memory read is a separate contract, not a permission hidden here.

M4b acceptance update — 2026-09-07: measurement-episode-read/0.1-candidate SHAPE ACCEPTED;
M3 key condition CLOSED. [M4a delayed opportunity revision1](CAMPAIGN2_MEASUREMENT_MEMORY_M4A_DRAFT.md)
is now proposed. Numeric allocation still awaits M4a/composed inventory; MEMR-A..P NOT PASSED.

- Equal permitted 337 content with different hidden causes gives equal memory and recall;
  any generic-component/public-exclusion split must remain explicit.
- Suppressed observation, another observer and unadmitted input cannot form or recall this memory.
  Missing evidence does not become a remembered negative measurement.
- Ablating the proposed memory formation or recall path removes the corresponding later response;
  inspecting trace/archive/REG or current probe output cannot stand in for memory access.
- Only the named memory authority changes its declared family. Beliefs, values, expectations,
  habits, relationships, person models and identity remain unchanged by this target.
- Later D, permission or calibration changes do not rewrite remembered historical content;
  restore, rollback and continuation retain exact provenance and deterministic behavior.
- Historical probe, carriage and X/E/L controls remain valid under their frozen models;
  a successor's scheduling/allocation noninterference must be specified and tested separately.
